WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:03.603
I was a Democrat for about 55 years.

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:06.306
And as governor, James

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:07.340
Burns of South

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.142
Carolina a few years ago said,

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:11.611
he said the Democratic Party didn't.

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:12.412
I didn't leave it.

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:15.215
It left me and I, I think that they moved

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:17.917
so far to the left in 1984

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:19.819
that I just couldn't go along and I,

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:21.054
I have been more at home

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:22.022
for a number of years

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:23.156
with the national platform

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:24.257
of the Republican Party

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:25.992
and I finally made it official.

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:26.693
Weren't you though

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:27.427
it would have been natural

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:28.561
to think you'd have supported

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:30.363
say Jimmy Carter

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:32.766
just on moral and religious grounds.

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:35.101
Well I supported him in the

00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:37.804
primary activity,

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:39.506
but I interviewed him

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:41.741
for my television program several days

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:42.842
before the election.

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:44.444
And after I'd had that experience,

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:45.979
I voted for Gerald Ford.

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:47.580
You were unimpressed

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.382
that I was unimpressed.

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:50.183
That's right.

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:51.084
Why do you think you'll

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:51.985
make a good president?

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.087
Well,

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:54.521
I love

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:55.321
people, and I

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:57.891
think that may be a very important thing.

00:00:57.924 --> 00:01:00.260
I have had 25 years of leadership.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:04.097
I, I built up an organization from $70

00:01:04.097 --> 00:01:04.764
until now.

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:05.732
We have

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:07.367
somewhere with stolen part time

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:09.335
employees over 3500 people.

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:11.304
We operating all around the world,

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:13.139
and I've been

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:14.441
feeding and clothing

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:15.842
the needy five

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:17.343
and a half million people last year.

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:17.510
We're

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:20.046
educating the people in the inner cities

00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:22.382
and in Appalachia how to read and write.

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:25.418
I have very broad foreign experience.

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:27.120
I've been to 44 countries

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.488
and I have been dealing

00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:30.123
with the issues of our world

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:31.524
now for at least ten years

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:32.292
on television

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:33.693
on a daily basis, practically.

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:35.328
So I am informed

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:37.097
and I do have a law degree

00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:38.298
and I'm

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:39.032
pretty much up

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:40.233
on the issues of the world,

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:41.234
but people are looking

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:42.202
for strong leadership,

00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:43.770
and I think I can give the point.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:45.805
Ken, can frankly, can religion

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:48.141
get in the way of politics?

00:01:48.141 --> 00:01:50.910
That is, can your religious beliefs,

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:53.913
which we respect, affect you in a

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:56.216
way that hurts politically?

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:57.951
Well, I think

00:01:57.951 --> 00:01:58.318
there's a

00:01:58.318 --> 00:01:59.953
misapprehension now

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:01.988
in the country about what

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:03.823
religious people feel.

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:05.592
I'm a student of history,

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:06.960
and I go back to the roots

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:07.660
of this nation.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:08.595
My family did.

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:09.262
And I

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:09.963
have studied

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:10.730
and I live here

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:11.564
in sort of the cradle

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:12.832
of the American democracy

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:14.434
in this part of Virginia.

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:15.902
And in those days,

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:17.203
the leaders of our country

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:18.771
were profoundly religious people.

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:20.073
George Washington.

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:21.808
John Adams.

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:22.675
Madison.

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:25.712
These men were deeply spiritual people.

00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:27.947
And I don't think our forefathers

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:28.848
intended religion

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:30.650
to be separated from the government,

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:32.452
but they just didn't want some big church

00:02:32.452 --> 00:02:33.620
trying to dominate them.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:35.221
They didn't want a federal church.

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:36.589
And I totally agree with that.

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:38.057
I don't think that the institution

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:39.659
or church as such

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:40.326
should be trying

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:41.761
to manipulate the government.

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:43.029
The government should be

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:43.830
should be neutral

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:44.931
in matters of religion,

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:48.001
and they should ensure freedom

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:49.235
for all people.

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:50.870
Right.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:51.171
Okay.

00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:51.604
Well, does that

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:52.839
mean that Pat Robertson

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:55.542
could vote for an atheist for president

00:02:55.542 --> 00:02:58.111
as long as he agreed with his policies?

00:02:58.111 --> 00:03:00.513
On things international and domestic?

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:03.516
I don't think that anybody

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:04.684
who doesn't believe in

00:03:04.684 --> 00:03:06.819
God really has his act together,

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:08.488
if I can say that honestly.

00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:09.222
You could not vote

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:11.024
for an atheist for president.

00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:12.125
I think he's

00:03:12.125 --> 00:03:13.593
missed a great part of reality.

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:14.427
I believe that

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:15.862
94% of the American people

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:16.563
believe in God,

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:18.398
and I think that that is essential

00:03:18.398 --> 00:03:19.832
to a responsibility.

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:20.433
You see,

00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:22.135
I have to give account to God

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:23.036
for everything I do.

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:24.737
I don't care if somebody sees me or not.

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:26.039
I have to give account to him.

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:27.307
But I'd like to know

00:03:27.307 --> 00:03:28.575
that people are in leadership

00:03:28.575 --> 00:03:30.043
positions who feel that

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:32.245
moral sense of constraint.

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:32.845
Why then do

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:33.413
you think

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:34.847
it would have to be a thought

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:37.250
that despite their own religious beliefs

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:38.017
and their desire

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:41.154
not to have a national church, they left

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:44.791
the word God out of the Constitution?

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:47.594
I was talking to

00:03:47.594 --> 00:03:48.061
one of the

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:48.661
students

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:50.363
from our public policy school

00:03:50.363 --> 00:03:53.833
at our university today, and he indicated

00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:57.337
that the early Congress required

00:03:58.204 --> 00:04:01.841
some type of affirmation of faith in God,

00:04:02.075 --> 00:04:03.910
of at least the Declaration

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:06.980
of Independence for all of the new states

00:04:07.013 --> 00:04:08.248
that join the territories

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:10.016
in the West and places like that.

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:10.283
Let's see.

00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:11.818
The Declaration of Independence

00:04:11.818 --> 00:04:14.320
is really part of our founding document,

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:17.223
and that talks about the laws of nature,

00:04:17.223 --> 00:04:18.091
but it's of God.

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:19.192
But it's not the law of the land.

00:04:19.192 --> 00:04:20.793
The Constitution is the law of the land.

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:21.127
And when they

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:21.761
was celebrating

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:22.395
that this year,

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:23.730
and I would think that the framers

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:24.964
had to be pretty careful

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:26.833
to leave out a word as important,

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:27.400
as you say

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:29.535
God must be, to leave it entirely

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:30.770
out of the Constitution.

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:32.538
Well, you know, in the transmittal letter

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:33.506
signed by George

00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:34.207
Washington,

00:04:34.207 --> 00:04:37.910
it said In the year of our Lord 1787.

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:39.679
So they did put it in the Constitution.

00:04:39.679 --> 00:04:41.881
In terms of the transmittal document,

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:43.049
I think that

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:44.417
it was

00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:45.585
understood that the

00:04:45.585 --> 00:04:47.186
declaration of Independence

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:48.755
was the framework

00:04:48.755 --> 00:04:50.490
in which the Constitution was written,

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:51.824
and it wasn't necessary

00:04:51.824 --> 00:04:53.192
to recite that over again.

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:53.459
All right.

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:55.561
Could you vote for a Jew for president?

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:56.396
Absolutely.

00:04:56.396 --> 00:04:57.297
I have

00:04:57.363 --> 00:04:59.866
the head of the Jewish Coalition

00:04:59.866 --> 00:05:00.400
for Reagan.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:01.901
Bush is working

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:03.469
as my assistant press secretary.

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:04.304
He left the White House

00:05:04.304 --> 00:05:05.204
to come to work for me.

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:05.905
He is a

00:05:05.905 --> 00:05:08.341
is a very wonderful conservative Jew.

00:05:08.341 --> 00:05:09.676
And I think like him

00:05:09.676 --> 00:05:11.177
on almost every issue, I'm

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:13.479
I'm very supportive of Jewish people

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:14.580
in this country and Jewish

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.182
people in Israel.

00:05:16.215 --> 00:05:17.150
Let's get into some things

